READING
==============================================================================
  At N=1000 the estimator's advantage is clear in a single draw.
  At the benchmark sample sizes the per-trial Improv straddles zero, so
  ONE draw cannot separate a real gain from a lucky one, in the paper's
  OWN simulator under assumptions kinder than a real LLM benchmark (no
  prompt sensitivity, no grading error, auxiliary signal informative).

  SCOPE, so this is not over-read: the simulator estimates theta =
  sigma^2, a variance; the tables report accuracy, a proportion. No
  numeric transfer between them is claimed. What this establishes is
  qualitative and independent of the tables: at N = 15-100 this
  estimator's per-draw advantage is not resolvable even under its own
  ideal DGP. The binomial argument addresses the published numbers.

